WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.462
- When we had McNabb on here, I didn't know 15 years later 
that you guys had not reconciled.

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:06.047
- Nah, I've tried. He's phony.

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:10.593
I tried to be cordial with the situation. I thought we had squashed it, 
but then you guys did an interview,

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:13.596
and then all this resurfaces again.

00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:19.644
♪♪♪ 

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:22.355
- So who we got in the pool hall today? 

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.690
Finally, T.O.!

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:23.940
Finally, T.O.!

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.482
- What's happenin'?

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:25.233
- What's good with you, man?

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:26.067
- I'm good, bro

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:26.693
- How you livin'?

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.404
- Just like everybody else during
this pandemic. Slow right now.

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:30.739
- [Laughing]

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:31.823
- I gotta ask you man:

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:32.866
How nice are you on the pool table?

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.869
Cuz the Untold Stories audience has been
waiting for you to jump on the pool table.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.456
- Well, you know, I ain't really come here to play no pool, but you know.

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:41.166
- Don't worry, the audience is getting their popcorn ready too.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:43.835
OK.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.086
- So I gotta to ask you, 

00:00:45.086 --> 00:00:47.505
Untold Stories' audience has been waiting for you to jump on this show. 

00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:48.089
- Right.

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:51.718
-After the Donovan McNabb episode, what was your reaction 
when you saw that episode?

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.345
- I mean, just listening to some of the comments and statements about

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:57.766
I "pretty much ruined the opportunity to run it back."

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:58.975
Leading up to the Super Bowl,

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:00.810
all the questions within the media, 

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.313
they were geared around, was I gonna make it back?

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:06.649
For him to be, really, the quarterback, the face of the franchise, 

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:08.777
I felt like he could've answered those questions. 

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:11.738
I guess for whatever reason, the statement of 

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.824
he didn't need me to win the Super Bowl or play in the Super Bowl, 

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.118
I felt that was a slight for whatever reason. 

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.703
And then I saw the interview—

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:22.040
- Like, it's unbelievable. But, you know, that was somethin' that 

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.708
kinda broke us up.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:26.336
That was the most frustrating for me because I knew 

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:28.004
what we could do

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:30.715
and if we decided to just come together, 

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:32.258
what we'd be able to accomplish.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.345
- He said that I ruined their chances, so for me, it was contradictory.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.639
To say that you didn't need me to play in the Super Bowl 

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:38.598
and win it, 

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.768
but then I prevented you guys from running it back.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.229
So you didn't need me then, so why would you need me to run it back?

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:47.357
For me, I felt like it was bush league to me, to be honest.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.027
- You out here playin' bumper pool.

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:55.990
- The '04 season. We heard McNabb's perspective in terms of 
how he felt that season played out. 

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.325
I wanna hear your perspective. 

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.952
How'd you feel the '04 season started?

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.996
- When I went over to the Philadelphia Eagles, I had 

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:05.542
nothing but the utmost respect for that organization.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:10.547
And for me to come over and add to the fire power that they already 
had with Donovan at the quarterback position—

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:14.509
in San Francisco, I didn't have a quarterback that could 
step back, you know, throw the ball 

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:16.427
80, 90 yards down the field. 

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:18.847
We had that in Donovan. I knew that going over there.

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:20.890
- 70-yard drop in the bucket, right?

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.226
- Yeah, I mean 81 yards, right on the jersey number.

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:25.645
- 81 yards, yeah.
- Right on the jersey number.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.272
- So '04 season started smooth, then?

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:29.149
- Oh, man, it started out with a banger. 

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.152
Going throughout the course of the season, there was no problems. 

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.111
There were no problems.

00:02:33.111 --> 00:02:35.196
The city of Philadelphia embraced me. 

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.490
Where I was at the height of my career at that time, 

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.950
I felt like I was unstoppable. 

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.535
I knew what I brought to the table. 

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:44.122
Everything was going according to plan, and then late December,

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:46.207
we're playing the Cowboys and that's when—

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:49.419
- I'm a Cowboys fan, man. So that play, I can never forget that play, man.

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:53.423
- Man, yeah, that play there, I mean, it changed a lot of things for

00:02:53.423 --> 00:02:56.384
really kinda the rest of the season for us and, you know, for the league.

00:02:56.384 --> 00:03:00.013
That play by Roy Williams, it got deemed as the horse collar rule.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.681
- So how long were they talking about you supposed to be out for?

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.684
- With that type of injury for any normal person, 

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.269
they're done for the rest of the season.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.646
I took that as a challenge, and I was like, "OK, cool. 

00:03:08.646 --> 00:03:09.772
Let's get with it." 

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:15.486
And I vowed at that time, I said, "If our team plays these playoffs and they win—"

00:03:15.486 --> 00:03:16.237
- I remember that.
- I said,

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:18.781
"I'll be ready for the Super Bowl. 

00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:21.409
I'll be ready." That’s what I—and I truly believed that.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:22.577
- How'd you perform? How'd you feel you did?

00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:24.871
- I didn't do bad, you know, considering—

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.788
- What were the stats again?

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.374
- Nine for 122. Nine for 122.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.460
- What happened against the Patriots?

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:33.922
- When you're a quarterback or any other position, 

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:37.050
do what got you there. You know, try not to do too much. 

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.218
I was tryna be perfect.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:42.805
And so some of the balls that—which I threw,
obviously—ended up bein’ intercepted. 

00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:45.350
In turnovers versus New England, 

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.394
it's tough because they always come back and capitalize.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:54.525
- There were some things that were said and known after the fact
about, you know, Donovan's play, things of that nature.

00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:55.109
- Like what?

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:56.527
- I mean, they said he threw up in the huddle.

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:58.446
- I need you to set the record straight.

00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:00.365
- I did not throw up in the game.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:01.324
- You did not throw up in the game?

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:02.325
- I did not throw up in the game.

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:03.201
- Where did this come from?

00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:05.912
- You know what, that’s a great question. 

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.331
As I say every time people bring it up,

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:10.416
roll the videotape. 

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.126
You know, the film don’t lie.

00:04:12.126 --> 00:04:13.336
- Why would somebody lie? 

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:15.588
There were teammates that said he threw up in the huddle.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.131
Personally, I didn't see it,

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:18.758
but there are guys, and I know that there are

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.551
teammates that I've talked to recently

00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:22.720
that said that they saw him throw up in the huddle. 

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.806
I've talked to teammates since then 

00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:27.892
and know for a fact that he was out the night before.

00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:28.685
- He was out the night before?

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:30.395
- Yeah, he was out the night before, 

00:04:30.395 --> 00:04:33.064
before the biggest game pretty much of all of our careers.

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:36.025
There's people that saw him out the night before, 

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:39.737
said he was drinking, and I think that attributed 
to him throwing up in the huddle. 

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:42.532
He's obviously had a history of condition problems.

00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:46.703
So, for me, you know, knowing all this information, I felt like that was irresponsible,

00:04:46.703 --> 00:04:50.915
especially for somebody of his caliber, his status,
to obviously be the leader of the team,

00:04:50.915 --> 00:04:55.545
and you're out the night before the biggest game of your career.
You're out drinking or what have you, 

00:04:55.545 --> 00:04:58.923
and then that maybe contributed to him throwing up in the huddle. 

00:04:58.923 --> 00:05:00.341
It’s just not good.

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:01.217
- Come on, scratch.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.261
-Yeah.

00:05:03.261 --> 00:05:05.054
- At this point, are you guys still cool?

00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:06.472
- Yeah.
- Like, when did things turn 

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.182
sour between you and McNabb?

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:11.477
- At this point, like, I had no problems with McNabb.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.896
I think things turned sour the next year.

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:18.359
Obviously there were some contract negotiations, some situations surrounding me. 

00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:20.403
Andy Reid and I, we had some disagreements.

00:05:20.403 --> 00:05:21.988
He sent me home for the day. 

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.115
He basically just told me to keep myself in shape, you know?

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:27.327
He'll get back in touch with me when he
feels like we're ready to resume or whatever.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:30.913
- Then all of a sudden, there’s turmoil here
and there are conversations going back and forth.

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:37.962
And we had to answer those questions instead of focusing on
what we need to do in order to get back to where we were.

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:38.796
- What ends up coming out of that?

00:05:38.796 --> 00:05:39.881
- So, I go home. 

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:43.551
I drive home. By the time I get home, obviously it's breaking news.

00:05:43.551 --> 00:05:47.638
It's basically hit the media wire that I'd been sent home or what have you.

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:50.600
And I’m in the house maybe 20, 30 minutes,

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.978
and next thing you know, I hear a knock at the door. I look through the blinds,

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:57.231
and media trucks are camped in my front yard.

00:05:57.231 --> 00:05:58.191
- What was going on in your mind?

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.360
that's not a normal experience for anybody. Even an athlete,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.153
like, that's not a normal experience for an athlete to have.
- Nah, it wasn't normal for me.

00:06:02.153 --> 00:06:04.238
Like I said, it was very unexpected.

00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:09.035
I just didn't understand what the hoopla was, I guess, surrounding me.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.829
I learned to embrace it, and I think that moment was

00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:19.295
me learning and trying to embrace the media. So that's why I came
out there with the ab bench and doin’ the situps and things of that nature. 

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:21.214
Because I tried to make light of the situation.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.174
I took it to heart that 

00:06:23.174 --> 00:06:26.928
Andy Reid said, he told me to stay in shape while I was away. So, I—

00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:28.179
- You just took it literally.

00:06:28.179 --> 00:06:30.223
- Yeah, literally. I did. I took it that way.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:33.184
- I thought that was the major distraction for us. 

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:39.190
You know, he’s doin’ situps. You know, he’s doin’ pushups.
He’s playin’ basketball. He’s ordering pizza for the people out there.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.652
And we sittin’ there in training camp just like, “You gotta be kiddin’ me!”

00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:45.863
- Honestly, if you look in that clip, I got an earpiece in my ear.

00:06:45.863 --> 00:06:47.532
I had my publicist on the line,

00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:52.912
and she's hearing everything that's going on. And so she's hearing
the questions, and she's basically telling me what to say.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:56.165
So, but I mean, it was just me having fun with that moment.

00:06:56.165 --> 00:06:57.333
- We in our dorm rooms

00:06:57.333 --> 00:07:00.586
and, you know, I’m just sittin’ there and I’m watchin’ on TV.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.214
And Brian Dawkins and Trotter were my roommates.

00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:05.925
And Dawkins come in. He’s like, “Man, what he do now?”

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:07.593
I'm like, "Take a look."

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.052
- [Laughing]

00:07:08.052 --> 00:07:09.554
- Like, this is like Days—
- Roll the footage.

00:07:09.554 --> 00:07:11.514
-This is like Days of our Lives.

00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:13.641
- Looking back on that, do you wish you could've
handled that differently or, like—?

00:07:13.641 --> 00:07:17.103
- Uh-uh. I mean, if it happened today, I would probably do the same thing.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:17.979
You know what I mean? 

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:22.233
I may have added some popcorn and some
little bit of everything at this point in time. 

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:24.944
Like, I really would've made it really a show.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.029
Speaking of popcorn, can I get some popcorn?

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:28.739
- I got you. I hope y'all got y’all popcorn ready

00:07:28.739 --> 00:07:29.407
for this one too.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:07:29.407 --> 00:07:31.826
you got to have your popcorn ready at all given times. 
- Gotta have the popcorn.

00:07:31.826 --> 00:07:33.244
Yeah, no doubt.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:36.998
- At that time, that was between me and Andy Reid. It was a disagreement. 

00:07:36.998 --> 00:07:38.040
He sent me home.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.709
What I do at my house is my business. 

00:07:39.709 --> 00:07:41.752
I don't worry about what you doin’ in your house.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:43.838
- And this point too, 

00:07:43.838 --> 00:07:45.298
so you're going through the contract situation. 

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:46.757
You mentioned earlier about McNabb. 

00:07:46.757 --> 00:07:50.094
What was his involvement in terms of your contract situation? 
What'd you hope that he would do?

00:07:50.094 --> 00:07:53.681
- Donovan, he was an advocate for Brian Westbrook getting his money.

00:07:53.681 --> 00:07:56.142
When it came to me, he wasn't as vocal.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:08:00.188
You don't talk about another man's pocket, you know what I mean? 
You don't talk about another man's money.

00:08:00.188 --> 00:08:05.151
But at the end of the day, he took the liberty to talk about 
and be an advocate for Brian's contract.

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:08.112
But then when it came to me, it was the polar opposite.

00:08:08.112 --> 00:08:10.072
So that's why I knew things had kinda changed.

00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:10.990
- Why do you think that was?

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.533
- I don't know. You should've asked him.

00:08:12.533 --> 00:08:17.497
For whatever reason, I guess it ate at him that people said
that I made him a better quarterback.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:20.291
Those are questions that the media had asked him,

00:08:20.291 --> 00:08:21.792
and he snapped back at ‘em.

00:08:21.792 --> 00:08:23.002
Be complimentary.

00:08:24.962 --> 00:08:26.756
- There you go. At that point, is that when the fallout is just so evident?

00:08:26.756 --> 00:08:31.052
- Yeah, I mean, think from that point, even from the Super Bowl 
with him answering the questions of, 

00:08:31.052 --> 00:08:33.221
he didn't need me to win the Super Bowl.

00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:36.974
- When we had McNabb on here, I didn't know 15 years later that you guys

00:08:36.974 --> 00:08:37.850
had not reconciled.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:38.768
- Nah, I've tried. 

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:40.311
I tried to be cordial 

00:08:40.311 --> 00:08:44.148
with the situation. I thought we had squashed it, 
but then you guys did an interview

00:08:44.148 --> 00:08:46.609
last year or whenever it was, some months ago. 

00:08:46.609 --> 00:08:49.070
And then all this resurfaces again.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.864
- Are you and T.O. on talkin’ terms, or what’s the relationship like now?

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:54.033
- Hey, I give a nice peace sign and keep it movin’.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:58.329
You know, I’ve—you know, I respect his time.
You know, I love my time.

00:08:58.329 --> 00:09:00.498
You know, and, and there's no need for me 

00:09:00.498 --> 00:09:04.835
to try to dust off anything that happened in the past
cuz what was in the past is in the past.

00:09:04.835 --> 00:09:07.964
You know, he's made a few comments, you know, as of late. 

00:09:07.964 --> 00:09:09.257
That's cool with me. 

00:09:09.257 --> 00:09:12.343
Listen, I’m a grown man. I handle grown-man business.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:16.347
- Will it ever be a point of reconciliation, you think? It’s been 15 years, 20 years.

00:09:16.347 --> 00:09:17.932
- I've heard him say he's moved on. 

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:19.225
He puts up the deuces.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.269
Bro, at the end of the day, he don't make me, man. 

00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:22.937
Like I said, I'm in the Hall of Fame

00:09:22.937 --> 00:09:24.605
for what I've done and what I've accomplished.

00:09:24.605 --> 00:09:27.149
I appreciate the opportunity to have played with him, 

00:09:27.149 --> 00:09:30.403
but at the end of the day, like I said, check my stats before I got there

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:33.030
and check my stats when I left.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:37.577
He's supposed to be the great quarterback or one
of the top quarterbacks in the league in his mind.

00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:40.371
You can't go to Washington and not beat out Rex Grossman.

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:43.124
- You think he belongs in the Hall of Fame?

00:09:43.499 --> 00:09:44.750
- I could care less.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.376
- [Laughing]

00:09:45.376 --> 00:09:48.379
At the end of the day, I'm worried about me. I could care less about that.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:50.673
- [Laughing]

00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:51.924
- Whoo!

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.342
I tried to—
- Put alot of heat on that one.

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:55.928
- Yeah, I tried to bring some sauce with that thing.

